Git safety rules
- Automation must never directly write unreviewed changes to the production branch.
- Every proposed update must be traceable.
- Avoid duplicate pull requests for identical changes.
- Use deterministic IDs and idempotent processing.
- Require checks before merging.
- Protect production branches.
- Preserve the previous verified resource when an update fails.
Pipeline state and fetched page snapshots should be stored outside the published content branch to avoid unnecessary commits.
9. Redirect system
FreeStack can provide resource-specific redirects such as:
/go/example-ai-api


Redirect workflow
1. Website build generates a slug-to-destination map from valid resource JSON.
2. Cloudflare Worker receives the redirect request.
3. Worker checks the slug against the generated map.
4. Worker redirects only to an approved HTTPS destination.
5. Click events can be recorded.
6. Unknown slugs fall back to the resource page or a not-found response.
Security rules
- No arbitrary redirect URLs supplied through query parameters.
- Only allowlisted HTTPS destinations.
- Reject malformed URLs and unsupported protocols.
- Avoid redirect chains.
- Never expose internal configuration or secrets.
